+// What threads free stays in the arenas and does not come back as address space of the system. An embedder that finds none
+// there keeps a piece of the arenas aside instead. A piece belongs to no thread and nothing is written to it.
+// The embedder calls these two from one thread at a time.
+#define MI_KEEPS_PIECES_ASIDE  1
+mi_decl_export bool mi_keep_piece_aside(size_t size) mi_attr_noexcept;     // false if there is no room for it
+mi_decl_export bool mi_release_piece_kept_aside(void) mi_attr_noexcept;    // the last one; false if there is none
+
 // For an interface that cannot say which of its requests can fail, and most of whose callers end the process on NULL.
 // As the functions without `must`, but a request that has found no memory asks once more as one that cannot fail.
 // NULL when that finds no memory either.
